WEBVTT

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.690
<i>Crossing the steal beam!</i>

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.940
<i>A psychotic game orchestrated by Teiai!</i>

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.060
<i>Victory means wealth. 
Defeat means a free fall...</i>

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.210
<i>and inescapable death!</i>

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.590
<i>But even then, they had 
no choice but to press on.</i>

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.040
<i>They stoke the faintest embers 
of hope within each other!</i>

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.130
<i>We now look back to a moment prior 
to this nightmarish evening...</i>

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.430
<i>After much difficulty,</i>

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.200
<b>Rock-Paper-Scissors</b>

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.200
<b>Card Game</b>

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.090
<i>the proposal for Restricted 
Rock-Paper-Scissors passes!</i>

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.930
<i>A victorious celebration leaves 
all involved intoxicated!</i>

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.070
<i>And then, every last man 
in black is late to work!</i>

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.820
<i>At the meeting the next day...</i>

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:54.570
<i>All their heads are shaven in remorse!</i>

00:00:54.570 --> 00:01:00.010
<i>All the names and faces Tonegawa 
had finally remembered are reloaded!</i>

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.950
<i>He has to learn them again!</i>

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.660
<i>Tonegawa Yukio,</i>

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.960
<i>the number two man of 
the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.650
<i>He serves the monster 
of the financial sector.</i>

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:16.970
<i>This shot-caller rose to the position 
of President Hyoudou's right-hand man.</i>

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:21.750
<i>This is the story of the battles 
he waged as a middle manager,</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.160
<i>in the shadows of the glory 
and fame he achieved...</i>

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:33.590
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
about the struggles of a remarkable man.</i>

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:44.120
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:44.120
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.160
Agenda 03
<b>Self-Destruct</b>

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.550
It's this one...

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.300
No, I think...

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:13.530
This is Yamazaki.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.420
Nagata

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.890
Who the hell can tell?!

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.350
<i>I thought they needed incentive,</i>

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:24.820
<i>not just reprimands, to make sure 
the project was a success...</i>

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:28.600
<i>But all that got me was sloth. 
They started slacking.</i>

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.860
<i>I'm not your mother.</i>

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:34.900
<i>It's my job to take control of you men</i>

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.610
<i>and guide you toward the project's success...</i>

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.040
<i>Like a jockey! It might be extreme,</i>

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.950
<i>but this could be a good 
chance to wake them up.</i>

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.440
<i>He chooses to saddle up!</i>

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.040
<i>With a change in policy, Tonegawa 
is now in extreme discipline mode!</i>

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:58.500
<i>And the next day, in Meeting Room 3...</i>

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.670
Today we begin preparations for the game.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:05.080
With the Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors 
event on the horizon,

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.380
we have a lot of things to take care of, 
and the first will be a venue.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:12.060
We need a location that'll be suitable 
for a diabolic game such as ours.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.430
Without that, we won't know what 
equipment we need, or how much.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:19.300
I want you all to work together 
and submit some good ideas.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.270
Yes, sir!

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.190
At least, that's what I thought at first...

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:24.570
But this time, we'll be having a contest.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.570
Ebitani

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.570
Doushita

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.570
Kawasaki

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.680
C-Contest?

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.570
<b>Psst...</b>

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.830
That's right. A contest.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.390
At the meeting three days from now, 
each of you will present your own idea.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:36.580
Suggestions for diabolical venues.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:42.090
Nagata                  Nakata                  Kikuchi

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:41.380
<b>Psst...</b>

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:41.450
And the one whose suggestion 
is accepted will be our winner.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.090
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:45.220
Knock down those around you!

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.430
Yamazaki

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.220
<b>Psst...</b>

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.850
Leave them behind!

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.410
If you don't win, you're trash!

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.540
There's no way for losers to survive!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.540
So, win!

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.230
<b>Psst...</b>

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.830
<i>Nothing good comes of</i>

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.460
<i>having you people working 
together in harmony.</i>

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:09.720
<i>Tonegawa was imagining something.</i>

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:14.250
<i>A narrow path in front him.</i>

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:20.880
<i>Around him were each of the men in 
black, each following a similar path.</i>

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:26.520
<i>They are too far apart to help each 
other, even if they wanted to.</i>

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:31.860
<i>There's no way of reaching anyone. 
Each is on his own.</i>

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:36.170
<i>Eleven points of light, marching along alone.</i>

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.390
<i>Every man for himself.</i>

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:42.390
<i>In the end, the bottom line is that 
people are fundamentally alone.</i>

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:46.370
<i>Trying to foster unity was a mistake.</i>

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.410
<b>Psst...</b>

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.090
A contest?

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:51.080
What're you gonna do?

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.410
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.620
<i>And then, three days later...</i>

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.630
<b>Meeting Room 3</b>

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.630
<i>The day of the contest arrives.</i>

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:08.130
Yamazaki

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:05.970
So, my suggestion for our venue

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.130
is the T.I. Event Hall.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:12.140
<b>T.I. Event Hall</b>

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:11.240
It's an event hall in Chuo,

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:14.140
and it's a spacious 450 square meters.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:18.670
Not only that, but the owner is a 
business partner under Teiai's control.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:21.030
That guarantees discretion.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.150
What do you think, sir?

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:24.920
It's not bad.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.070
But it's a bit run-of-the-mill.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.910
It has no devilish aspects 
or sense of shock.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:31.280
Next!

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.900
Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.840
<i>But even after that...</i>

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.790
My idea is for us to do it at an 
elementary school playground.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.900
That'd be surprising, 
but there'd be no secrecy!

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.240
You think we're running a field day?!

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:44.190
Next!

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:49.220
Nakata

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.850
U-Uh, well...

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:49.220
Could we maybe do it here in the meeting 
room, where we've got plenty of secrecy?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.840
There's not enough room!

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.350
And frankly, I'm amazed you 
had the guts to suggest this!

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:54.540
Uh, well...

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:54.970
Next!

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.470
My idea is to do it at a haunted location!

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.470
<b>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors Venue Proposal
Haunted Locations</b>

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:59.730
<b>Graveyard At Night</b>

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.730
How about a graveyard at night?

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:02.350
In that case, we could do 
it at an abandoned school!

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.360
If we use an automated train station, 
it'll be empty once the trains stop!

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.110
A bowling alley after hours!

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.110
Kikuchi

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.110
Th-Then I'd like to suggest...

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.490
Gutter balls!

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.830
<i>Not only was there a suggesting 
involving a bowling alley,</i>

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.450
<i>but none of the suggestions were a strike,</i>

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:22.370
<i>and only two men remain!</i>

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:25.190
<i>One is the creator of Restricted 
Rock-Paper-Scissors,</i>

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.490
<i>the youngest member and the hope 
of the team, Saemon-saburou!</i>

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.890
<i>The other is Ebitani, who was 
hired around the same time!</i>

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.890
You're next, Saemon.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.000
Yes, sir.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:45.400
Come to think of it, you're the only 
one who didn't shave his head...

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:47.570
Oh, right.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:51.030
I think mistakes made at work are best 
made up for with efforts at work.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.030
<b>Psst...</b>

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.970
Now, then...

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.170
<i>Here it comes again... PP!</i>

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.670
<b>What makes a demonic venue?</b>

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.170
<b>Psst...</b>

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.530
<b>Evil</b>

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.530
<b>What we need: Risk management</b>

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.990
<b>Demon</b>

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.990
<b>And a business model that
gives rise to irrepressible synergy</b>

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.180
Saemon-saburou Jirou presents:

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.180
<b>A Restricted-Rock-Paper-Scissors
Venue Proposal</b>

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:26.060
That being the case, 
my suggestion for our venue is:

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:29.070
The luxury liner <i>Espoir</i>!

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.070
<b>Luxury Liner Espoir</b>

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:30.610
A boat?

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.680
Yes, sir.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.660
I propose we rent a boat and hold the 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors game onboard.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:39.000
I've got the details outlined here.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:40.440
Ton-san.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.490
The Espoir weighs in at 60,000 tons.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:49.380
It's an extremely luxurious vessel, 
spanning over 300 meters.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:53.130
<b>Psst...</b>

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.640
What a pretty picture...

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:53.130
It's like we're really there...

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:57.540
Plus, it's owned by Kurogane 
Maritime, a Teiai subsidiary,

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.640
so there's no need to worry about secrecy.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.890
There's ample room, as well. 
The main hall is a robust 400 square meters!

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:05.390
<i>Th-This is...</i>

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:06.850
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.520
<i>4K?!</i>

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:12.810
Plus, the shock that comes from it 
being revealed as a gambling cruise!

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:15.100
There's no way to escape.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.120
A demonic cage, swirling 
with hope and despair.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.030
Which means...

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.290
the president will be delighted!

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.790
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.420
Excellent. I see.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.590
A gambling cruise is the perfect curve ball.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.920
I love it.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:36.680
Thank you, sir!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.960
<i>Once again, his PP has been unleashed!</i>

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:41.310
<i>And...</i>

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.430
<i>4K!</i>

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:48.930
<i>At this moment, Tonegawa, along with all 
the men in black, including Ton-san,</i>

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:51.940
<i>were certain that Saemon's 
proposal would be the right one!</i>

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.570
Okay, you're our closer, Ebitani.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.820
Yes, sir!

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.070
<i>With one exception!</i>

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.480
And now, to wrap things up,

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:05.830
I'm going to start passing 
out the documentation.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:08.330
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:13.710
<b>Ebitani Presents:
100 Reasons Why the Minami-Aoyama 
Japanese Restaurant Takumi Should Be the
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors Venue</b>

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:13.710
As you can see from the cover, 
my suggestion for our venue

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.410
is the Japanese restaurant, 
Takumi, in Minami-Aoyama.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:18.470
A... restaurant?

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.970
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:23.350
If you'll flip to the next page...

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:27.600
<b>Maruoka Junpei</b>

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.080
You'll see the "artisan" 
behind the name "Takumi."

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:30.600
The iron man at the head of the Japanese 
food scene, the owner, Maruoka Junpei.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.890
He's a straight-shooter, a hard-headed 
old man who's 100% dedicated to cooking,

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.610
but his skills are unrivaled.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:47.140
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:43.050
Despite its convenient location, the 
120-square-meter space of the restaurant

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.020
Ebitani...

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:43.040
Hey... Is he...

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:46.790
creates a cozy atmosphere that lets 
you forget the bustle of the city.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:49.120
<i>Th-This man...</i>

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.530
Plus, there's a private 
stall for the president,

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.710
<i>It's already obvious... the three 
factors needed for our venue...</i>

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:54.710
where the servers can take 
excellent care of him....

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:58.220
<i>This place doesn't fulfill 
a single one of them!</i>

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:05.970
<i>Ebitani manages a hat trick of failure!</i>

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:08.820
<i>Come to think of it, Ebitani was the one</i>

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:13.480
<i>who sent me that weirdly aggressive 
New Year's card when I was in mourning.</i>

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:14.650
<i>Happy New Year.</i>

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:18.490
<i>I'm going to work hard so I can claim 
the number two position at Teiai.</i>

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:25.450
<b>Maruoka Junpei's passion for 
creating Japanese cuisine (Long Interview)
"To me, a cutting board is like a blank canvas."</b>

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:23.130
<i>The amount of work here... the enthusiasm...</i>

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:25.470
<i>Yes. He's definitely enthusiastic.</i>

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:26.810
<i>He is, and yet...</i>

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:30.460
Now, reason 27 why I'm suggesting Takumi...

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:31.960
Its smoking section.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:35.960
<i>He's off-point! This man named Ebitani</i>

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.670
<i>is missing something fundamentally 
necessary to succeed!</i>

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.930
Reason 28: they've got space 
hollowed out beneath the tables.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:47.930
Reason 99: they offer 
tissues for delicate noses.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:00.820
Ebitani.

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:02.980
Sensei?

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:05.240
Overtime keeping you here this late?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.340
Yeah...

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:10.050
It's a shame your proposal 
didn't turn out better.

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:11.370
Well...

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:15.250
How about it? Care to go for a drink?

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:18.750
<b>Takumi</b>

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.940
Maybe in Minami-Aoyama.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.520
I see. This really is a pretty nice place.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:35.170
I know, right?

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.440
Yes. A nice restaurant,

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:39.600
but too small.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:40.900
Oh... right.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.910
Even beyond that, it's a terrible choice,

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:46.160
especially if this owner really 
is such a straight-shooter.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.410
Huh? Why?

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:53.660
You fool. We're orchestrating some 
extremely extra-legal gambling.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.800
It's about as far from the 
straight and narrow as it gets.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:02.060
Size. Secrecy. Surprise.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:04.950
The meetings conveyed that those 
were the three crucial factors.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:05.800
It was the subtext.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.430
Did you not notice at all?

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:09.550
I'm sorry.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:14.330
Well, in a way, your suggestion 
was the most surprising.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.080
Thank you, sir!

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:19.340
Don't let it go to your head, fool.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:21.110
It was surprising in the wrong way.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:23.760
Not to mention how you were going overboard!

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:24.990
A hundred reasons?

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.840
The president is one thing,

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:32.410
but we're going to have a group of debtors 
who will be in serious trouble if they lose.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:36.000
They don't need things like hollowed out 
leg space or bidets in their commodes!

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:37.700
Sorry, sir.

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:40.020
Forget it. Just sit down.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:46.760
It's just... lately, I feel sort of pressured, 
and nothing turns out right...

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:49.190
Is this about Saemon?

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:53.140
He's got you worried because 
of his performance, right?

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:55.780
<i>Psst...</i>

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.110
That guy...

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:00.900
He's younger than me, but we 
were hired around the same time.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:04.950
I thought he was just some annoying 
clown who does whatever he wants,

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:08.150
but he's earned far more 
recognition than me...

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:10.370
Ebitani.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.310
Do you know <i>why</i> you and 
that annoying clown who does

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:14.920
whatever he wants are different?

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:19.170
Hairstyle?

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.170
Wrong! Sense of scale.

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.170
S-Scale?

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:26.680
Yes. When he suggests an idea,

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:29.430
he doesn't consider small 
details like budgets and such.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:34.120
Meanwhile, you focus on things like 
what kind of legroom is available...

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:37.310
It felt like you were suggesting 
a restaurant for a party.

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.750
You're thinking on too small a scale!

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.820
Don't bother wasting your 
energy on minor details!

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.320
I'll handle that sort of thing!

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:51.070
<i>He impresses! With his overwhelming 
manliness as a boss!</i>

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:53.080
In one week, we're having a contest

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:55.830
for the design of the 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors cards.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.580
I expect you to shock me!

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.830
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:06.970
<i>Yes. I think his only problem 
is that he's off-mark.</i>

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:10.790
<i>He has more enthusiasm than anyone on 
the team, but his aim isn't correct.</i>

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:13.600
<i>It's a shame. In a sense, he's...</i>

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:15.000
Not this way!

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.110
What are you aiming at?!

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:17.220
Hey, other way! Turn around!

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.270
<i>...a cannon that's pointed the wrong way!</i>

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:24.000
<i>But if I can get him on target,</i>

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:28.070
<i>he could be as strong a leader 
for the team as Saemon!</i>

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.030
Tonegawa-sensei.

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:33.880
Thank you for tonight, sir.

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:36.510
I'm going to do my best!

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:39.270
I'll shock you! I'm sure of it!

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:43.080
Will you, now? I'll look forward to it.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:43.860
Yeah!

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:51.930
<i>The image that Tonegawa had seen when 
conceptualizing these contests...</i>

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:58.150
<i>Eleven points of light. 
They are each separate, indeed.</i>

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:01.430
<i>And that will never change, 
with each going down his own path.</i>

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:05.060
<i>But the one thing they can do to interact...</i>

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:08.950
<i>is communicate.</i>

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.560
<i>Words that cross the 
distance in the darkness.</i>

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:15.350
<i>An infinite exchange of ideas. 
Even if the paths never intermingle,</i>

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.830
<i>their words can reach out to each other.</i>

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:26.670
<i>Of course,</i>

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:29.640
<i>no one knows for certain</i>

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.550
<i>if those signals will be received correctly.</i>

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.840
<i>But by speaking to one another,</i>

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:38.170
<i>one man can change another.</i>

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:41.470
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.980
What's the fuss about?

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:48.160
Well, it's Ebitani... 
He hasn't shown up for work.

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:49.350
Ebitani?

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:52.110
Oh, don't worry. I heard from him.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.860
He called off today to deal 
with some personal affairs.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:57.110
But I'm worried, sir.

00:16:57.110 --> 00:17:00.120
Maybe he's depressed about how his 
presentation went yesterday...

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:03.870
Are you really that confident, Saemon?

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:05.370
<b>Psst...</b>

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:09.630
I see things another way.

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:13.630
Right now, Ebitani...

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:19.640
is waiting in a cauldron in the depths of hell 
for an opportunity to pull himself up.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:24.050
And I think that opportunity will be the 
contest for the design of the cards.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:28.150
Ebitani will give birth to something 
that will shock us all...

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:29.900
A demonic concept!

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:31.650
<b>Psst...</b>

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:36.700
I never even considered it...

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.610
Could it be?

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:39.530
You sound like a prophet!

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:44.330
I just have a grasp on 
how my employees think.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:49.590
President Hyoudou should be back 
from Hawaii any moment now.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.880
I should head to the airport to pick him up.

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:54.880
<i>Tonegawa astonishes even further!</i>

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.550
<i>With his absolute confidence as the boss!</i>

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:11.060
<i>If he's in a good mood, I'll ask him 
to approve the venue we decided on.</i>

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:14.490
<i>If not... it'll be untouchable.</i>

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.670
Fired!

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:19.320
<i>He's here!</i>

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:21.320
That pilot! He's fired!

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:21.970
Yes, sir!

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:25.330
The flight was too bumpy! 
Can't he handle a little turbulence?

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.490
Yes, sir! We'll arrange for it at once!

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:29.130
Damn right you will!

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:32.840
<i>This is bad! The gauge of the president's 
mood, the angle of his eyebrows...</i>

00:18:33.350 --> 00:18:36.010
<i>They're far beyond the 
safe range of 40 degrees!</i>

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:39.340
<i>He's in the absolute fury of the red zone!</i>

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:44.350
<i>The smart move here is to not do anything, 
and wait for another opportunity.</i>

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.980
Ebitani

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:47.980
<i>Psst...</i>

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:49.230
<i>Ebitani?!</i>

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:49.760
<i>Wha—</i>

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:51.930
<i>What are you doing here?!</i>

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:56.880
<i>A smothering anxiety seizes 
Tonegawa's chest,</i>

00:18:56.880 --> 00:19:02.870
<i>like his heart has been clenched 
by a pair of ice-cold hands!</i>

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.370
Hey, wait!

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.370
What do you want?!

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:11.120
President Hyoudou!

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:15.500
I'm Ebitani, and I have 
a request for you. sir!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:19.510
I'd like to get your handprints for 
rock, paper, and scissors designs!

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:22.510
So that they can be used for Restricted RPS!

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:23.940
<i>Psst...</i>

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:25.510
Please, sir!

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:30.520
<b>Psst...</b>

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:28.410
The president's handprints?

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:29.750
For cards?

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:31.690
Yes!

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:33.020
<b>Psst...</b>

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:36.020
<b>Psst...</b>

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:37.530
<b>Psst...</b>

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:41.160
You're fired!

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:43.720
<i>And Ebitani is out!</i>

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:44.530
<i>After only one strike!</i>

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:46.660
N-No way...

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:50.540
T-T-Tonegawa-sensei!

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:52.420
I-Idiot! Don't look over here!

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:58.050
Oh, President! H-How was Hawaii, sir?

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:00.720
Your pay is cut!

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:05.970
<i>His aim was altered through communication,</i>

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:09.970
<i>but a little too much...</i>

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:11.730
<i>resulting in self-destruction!</i>

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:23.740
<i>Eleven lights... reduced to ten!</i>

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.990
<i>Tonegawa makes a huge miscalculation!</i>

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:32.500
That was too much of a surprise, idiot!

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:41.800
Sensei?

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:43.590
Good morning.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:44.800
What are you, stupid?!

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:45.680
Sensei...

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:49.910
You got what you deserved... This goes 
beyond barking up the wrong tree!

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:51.810
And if anything...

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:51.810
<b>Psst...</b>

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:55.770
<i>I'm</i> the one who has the right to haunt <i>you</i>!

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:55.770
<b>Psst...</b>

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:56.080
Sensei...

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.110
Living Ghost

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.770
<b>Psst...</b>

00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:59.690
Go away! Leave me be!

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:02.520
Never show your face to me again!

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:04.200
What are you saying, Tonegawa-sensei?

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.900
Begone! Go away!

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:10.320
<i>This is the story of a lone man who 
struggles between his employer,</i>

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:10.320
Never show yourself to me again!

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:11.260
Sensei...

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:15.300
<i>the president, and the living ghost of 
one man in black who he employed....</i>

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:13.370
Go! Leave me!

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:14.210
Sensei...

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:17.270
Go away!

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:19.110
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:19.920
Leave me!

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:57.450
Next time: "Proliferation."

00:22:56.540 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Proliferation</b>
